# Tier 1, trixie main. The graphical stack minus the Hyprland packages
# themselves, which come from backports (see packages/backports.list).

# terminal (D6)
kitty

# bar, launcher, notifications
waybar
fuzzel
mako-notifier       # NB: binary package is mako-notifier, not mako

# wayland utilities
wl-clipboard
cliphist
grim
slurp
swappy
swaybg
wlr-randr
wtype
wf-recorder        # required by omakeb-capture-screenrecording

# hardware controls
brightnessctl
playerctl
pamixer
pavucontrol

# audio
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber

# The command-line mixers. pavucontrol above is the GUI, and shipping only the
# GUI is what made a real fault on the test machine hard to find: the volume
# meter moved, the right device was selected, and the headphones were silent —
# because the mute was in the ALSA hardware mixer, one layer below anything
# PipeWire will show you. There was no tool installed that could look there.
#
#   alsa-utils        amixer, alsamixer, aplay, speaker-test
#   pulseaudio-utils  pactl, pacmd — the pipewire-pulse side
#
# omakeb-hw-audio needs amixer; without it the check degrades to what PipeWire
# alone can see, which is precisely the layer that reports success.
alsa-utils
pulseaudio-utils

# network + bluetooth
network-manager
network-manager-gnome
bluez
blueman

# session plumbing
greetd
tuigreet            # NB: package is "tuigreet", not "greetd-tuigreet"
polkitd
mate-polkit         # lightweight polkit agent; no KDE/GNOME session pulled in
gnome-keyring
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-user-dirs
qt6-wayland
libnotify-bin

# applications
thunar
imv
mpv

# browser (D13)
#
# Debian names it firefox-esr, not firefox. It is here because a desktop with no
# browser is not a desktop: five learn.* rows in menu/menu.jsonc call
# omakeb-launch-browser, and on a fresh machine there was nothing for them to
# open — they reached the "No browser found" notification instead.
#
# It is the FALLBACK, not the preference. omakeb-launch-browser and
# omakeb-launch-webapp both try chromium first, because Chromium's --app gives a
# real chromeless window and Firefox has had no equivalent since --app was
# removed. Install chromium and it takes over with no configuration at all.
firefox-esr

# fonts + icons
#
# JetBrains Mono is the only family omakeb ever names. Font family is an omakeb
# constant and never a theme token, so a theme
# cannot ask for a face that is not installed; test/lint-fonts.py asserts that
# every family named in templates/ and default/ is provided by a package here.
fonts-jetbrains-mono

# The rest is COVERAGE, not style, and it is the reason this section grew.
# Without it anything outside JetBrains Mono's own repertoire renders as tofu
# boxes everywhere at once — filenames in thunar, window titles in the bar,
# notification bodies, web pages — and nothing anywhere reports it. Silent
# degradation is this project's recurring hazard; this is its font-shaped face.
#
#   noto-core    Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari, Thai and the rest
#                of the non-CJK world
#   noto-cjk     Chinese, Japanese, Korean. Much the largest thing in the base
#                install; delete this one line if disk matters more than the
#                tofu, nothing depends on it
#   dejavu-core  a guaranteed proportional face so fontconfig's `sans-serif`
#                alias resolves to something. GTK asks for sans-serif by
#                default and a netinst with no desktop task may ship no
#                proportional font at all
#   color-emoji  emoji, in the menu and in notifications
fonts-noto-core
fonts-noto-cjk
fonts-dejavu-core
fonts-noto-color-emoji

papirus-icon-theme
